cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "spnn-shortest-path: stochastic spiking networks for shortest-path computation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, data, and figures for the paper on stochastic spiking
  neural networks for shortest-path computation. A weighted graph is compiled into
  winner-take-all neuron clusters whose Boltzmann energy minima coincide with
  shortest paths and run as a discrete-time Boltzmann sampler at O(|E|) cost per step.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Engler
    given-names: Gary R.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - shortest-path
  - spiking-neural-network
  - boltzmann-machine
  - stochastic-neural-algorithms
